WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.621
Learn to identify the unknown in a problem, represent the problem with an equation,

00:00:05.621 --> 00:00:10.268
and solve the problem concretely, pictorially or symbolically and represent and solve

00:00:10.268 --> 00:00:14.915
a given addition or subtraction problem involving a “part- part-whole” or comparison

00:00:14.915 --> 00:00:18.013
context, using a symbol to represent the unknown

00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:25.397
30 pencils are in two boxes. One box has 8. Solve n plus 8 equals 30. The answer is

00:00:25.397 --> 00:00:28.147
22. Subtract the known part from the whole.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:34.222
Two friends have 33 balls altogether. One has 6. Write the missing amount. Pause and

00:00:34.222 --> 00:00:36.331
solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.616
The answer is 27. 33 minus 6 equals 27.
